invariant: INV-66
file: src/p256_adx_asm.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh p256-adx
reason: p256_adx_mul_mont's second round of the reduction drops the carry
  the first round left past its fifth word, so a product whose first round
  carries comes out short by 2^256 / 2^128 times that bit, a value no
  longer congruent to the product. The square keeps the carry, so only
  products go wrong, in about one product in four.
  bin/p256_adx_equiv_test compares each product with the model word for
  word, and the qemu lane runs it for x86-64.

